**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/

# Local configuration and secrets
.env
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
*.user

# Local databases
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Editors
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Messages the file mailer writes in development. Correspondence, and not
# something to commit.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, which is the whole point of this line. Written
# as "mail/" it matched any directory of that name at any depth, and on Windows
# git folds case when it matches an ignore pattern — so it swallowed
# src/JiranisokoTech.Application/Mail and src/JiranisokoTech.Infrastructure/Mail
# along with their tests. Nothing complained: the working copy built and every
# test passed, while the commit went out without two modules in it and the
# repository could not be built from a fresh clone.
/mail/

# Candidate CVs written by the file store. Documents belonging to people
# outside this firm, and not something to commit. Anchored for the same reason
# as above, before somebody adds a Cvs folder to the source.
/cvs/

# Worktrees the agent tooling creates. Not part of the project.
.claude/worktrees/
